<title>USA: Sanders gets $8.9 mln U.S. Navy contract.</title>
<headline>Sanders gets $8.9 mln U.S. Navy contract.</headline>
<dateline>NASHUA, N.H. 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanders of Lockheed Martin Corp said Wednesday it had received an $8.9 million contract from the U.S. Department of the Navy to develop an antenna system for some of its ships.</p>
<p>The company said the system will replace shipboard topside antennas.</p>
<p>It is to complete to project by September 1999, it said.</p>
<p>Sanders is an operating unit of the Lockheed Martin Electronics Sector, which designs, develops and manufactures electronics systems for the aerospace and defense markets.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
